; on the right side of `def`, a declared operator isn't new before its first use (the comma is
; declared in the core), and a symbol that wasn't declared is introduced as on any line -- the
; definition only names the term, so it stays conservative; the left side keeps exactly one new
; symbol, and the right side no other variables
load equality
brackets ⟨ ⟩
const b
def q = ⟨b, b⟩
q = ⟨b, b⟩
def r = g b
r = g b
